# Gunther Arasek of the Arasek Stockyard, at his stall in the square (docs/voice/gunther_arasek.md).

~ start
if not flag.arasek_met
set arasek_met
Narrator: A broad man in a leather apron stands behind a stall of blades, mail and coils of rope, with a ledger chained to the counter so nobody can walk off with the prices.
Gunther: Arasek Stockyard. Steel, leather, rope, grain. Everything that comes into Vallaki on a cart comes past me first, and the wolves get a look at it on the way.
else
Gunther: Back for more? Good. Steel doesn't sell itself. It mostly sits there being heavy.
endif
* Show us what you have. -> trade
* Why are your prices so steep? -> prices
* What's the news on the roads? -> roads
* Goodbye. -> END

~ trade
shop
Gunther: Pleasure. Bring it back dented and I'll buy it for half. Bring it back bloody and I'll buy it for less.
-> END

~ prices
Gunther: Twice what you'd pay over the mountains. Every cart that reaches us loses a horse or a driver on the way, some months both. My sister Yelena keeps the books, and the books say twice.
if name:kip_smudgewick
interject name:kip_smudgewick: Could the books say once and a half, neighbour? Trade rate? One merchant to another?
else
interject tag:curious: Could the books say once and a half?
endif
Gunther: You can ask Yelena. I'd sell you a helmet first.
if flag.bildrath_robbed
Gunther: You've come from the village, eh? Bildrath's prices? Ten times. And I hear somebody helped themselves to his strongbox. Not that I'd ever think it of you.
endif
-> start_menu

~ start_menu
* Show us what you have. -> trade
* What's the news on the roads? -> roads
* Goodbye. -> END

~ roads
Gunther: West road to Krezk: wolves, and worse past the river. The lake road: fishermen who've stopped catching anything and gone strange with it. East road, the way you came: an old windmill nobody sane stops at.
if flag.bonegrinder_rumor
interject tag:blunt: The windmill. We heard the old pastry woman bakes there.
Gunther: Then you heard right. My carters won't water their horses within sight of it. Horses go in. Horses don't come out.
endif
if flag.mists_wolves_cowed
Gunther: You came over the pass and the wolves let you by? Huh. They don't let my carts by.
endif
-> start_menu
